= Lenin Falls Silent

On 10 March Lenin suffers a third stroke. He lives, at Gorki, but he cannot speak and will not write again. Zinoviev and Kamenev have joined the general secretary, Stalin, against Trotsky. Radek, who knows Germany best, belongs to nobody.

The Zentrale's monthly report goes to the Executive. Somebody there has to read it first.

- @zinoviev: Send it to Zinoviev, the President.
- @trotsky: Send it to Trotsky.
- @radek: Send it to Radek.

@zinoviev
subtitle: The President likes to be asked. He likes the Left better.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -4);
Q.e23_patron = 1;
Q.independence -= 3;
!}

Zinoviev answers the report himself, at length, with compliments for the Berlin district.

@trotsky
subtitle: Trotsky wants a German revolution and a date for it. The triumvirs keep a list of who writes to him.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
Q.e23_patron = 2;
!}

Trotsky sends the reports back with questions in pencil about rifles, railway junctions and the sergeants of the Reichswehr.

@radek
subtitle: Radek will defend us in Moscow. Nobody there defends Radek.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
Q.e23_patron = 3;
!}

Radek promises to keep the German question out of the Russian one. He knows he cannot.
